  {
   "id": "sn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1130,
   "y": 130,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100104,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700728,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The volume gap between those two blue tables is the whole sharding story: millions\nof exposure events a day against about 1.35 million total live summary rows. The\nsame 'raw event volume dwarfs its own aggregate' shape as ad-click aggregation\nand payments.",
   "originalText": "The volume gap between those two blue tables is the whole sharding story: millions\nof exposure events a day against about 1.35 million total live summary rows. The\nsame 'raw event volume dwarfs its own aggregate' shape as ad-click aggregation\nand payments.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "sn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1130,
   "y": 216,
   "width": 576,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100105,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700735,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Both shard by experiment_id - matching the dominant query for each ('this\nexperiment's exposures', 'this experiment's metric curve') and, just as\nimportantly, keeping the (experiment_id, user_id) UNIQUENESS CONSTRAINT\nENFORCEABLE WITHIN A SINGLE SHARD rather than needing a cross-shard check.\nSharding either by a hash of user_id instead would scatter one experiment's\npopulation across every shard, turning both the join AND the dedup check into\ncross-shard operations.",
   "originalText": "Both shard by experiment_id - matching the dominant query for each ('this\nexperiment's exposures', 'this experiment's metric curve') and, just as\nimportantly, keeping the (experiment_id, user_id) UNIQUENESS CONSTRAINT\nENFORCEABLE WITHIN A SINGLE SHARD rather than needing a cross-shard check.\nSharding either by a hash of user_id instead would scatter one experiment's\npopulation across every shard, turning both the join AND the dedup check into\ncross-shard operations.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "sn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1130,
   "y": 346,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100106,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700742,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the replica-versus-shard distinction, again: replicas solve read throughput\nfor reporting and ad hoc audit queries against exposures; sharding solves the\nwrite volume and total size of exposures itself. Reaching for one when the other\nis the actual bottleneck is the mistake to avoid.",
   "originalText": "And the replica-versus-shard distinction, again: replicas solve read throughput\nfor reporting and ad hoc audit queries against exposures; sharding solves the\nwrite volume and total size of exposures itself. Reaching for one when the other\nis the actual bottleneck is the mistake to avoid.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
