   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "an EXPERIMENT whose ranges shift mid-run\n  a user drifts from control's range into treatment's;\n  both behaviours attribute to whichever arm fired  <- contamination",
   "originalText": "an EXPERIMENT whose ranges shift mid-run\n  a user drifts from control's range into treatment's;\n  both behaviours attribute to whichever arm fired  <- contamination",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "expt",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 944,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100113,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700791,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "It is the same hash-boundary-shift mechanic in both cases, and a feature-flag rollout leans on it INTENTIONALLY: growing a\nrange only adds users at the new edge, never reassigns users already inside it. For an experiment, that same behaviour means a\nuser's behaviour under control AND their behaviour under treatment both get attributed to whichever arm they happened to be in\nwhen a conversion event fired - contaminating the exact comparison the system exists to make.",
   "originalText": "It is the same hash-boundary-shift mechanic in both cases, and a feature-flag rollout leans on it INTENTIONALLY: growing a\nrange only adds users at the new edge, never reassigns users already inside it. For an experiment, that same behaviour means a\nuser's behaviour under control AND their behaviour under treatment both get attributed to whichever arm they happened to be in\nwhen a conversion event fired - contaminating the exact comparison the system exists to make.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1042,
   "width": 995,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100114,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700798,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "So bucket_start and bucket_end are computed once, from the allocation percentages in effect the moment start is called, and\nnever touched again for that experiment. Same technique, opposite verdict, from one differing requirement.",
   "originalText": "So bucket_start and bucket_end are computed once, from the allocation percentages in effect the moment start is called, and\nnever touched again for that experiment. Same technique, opposite verdict, from one differing requirement.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
