   "versionNonce": 700868,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "experiments(status, started_at)                   'which experiments are currently running' - the query every scheduled\n                                                  analysis sweep and every guardrail cycle runs. The same (status, timestamp)\n                                                  composite reasoning as the job scheduler's due-jobs scan.\nexperiment_variants(experiment_id)                every assignment-config load and every analysis run reads all of one\n                                                  experiment's variants together. No index on variant_key alone, because it is\n                                                  never queried without an experiment_id.\nUNIQUE exposures(experiment_id, user_id)          the concurrency-safety mechanism above, doubling as the aggregator's join\n                                                  index\nsummaries(experiment_id, variant_key,             the COMPOSITE PRIMARY KEY, matching ad-click aggregation's (ad_id,\n          metric_name, day)                       window_start) reasoning exactly: the dominant read is 'this experiment's\n                                                  per-variant metric curve over time', so the key itself serves the query with\n                                                  no secondary index. experiment_id FIRST is the leftmost-prefix point - it is\n                                                  what lets a single-experiment read jump straight to its rows without\n                                                  touching any other experiment's.\nsrm_checks(experiment_id, checked_at)             'this experiment's most recent SRM check' - the only pattern that ever runs\n                                                  against this table",
   "originalText": "experiments(status, started_at)                   'which experiments are currently running' - the query every scheduled\n                                                  analysis sweep and every guardrail cycle runs. The same (status, timestamp)\n                                                  composite reasoning as the job scheduler's due-jobs scan.\nexperiment_variants(experiment_id)                every assignment-config load and every analysis run reads all of one\n                                                  experiment's variants together. No index on variant_key alone, because it is\n                                                  never queried without an experiment_id.\nUNIQUE exposures(experiment_id, user_id)          the concurrency-safety mechanism above, doubling as the aggregator's join\n                                                  index\nsummaries(experiment_id, variant_key,             the COMPOSITE PRIMARY KEY, matching ad-click aggregation's (ad_id,\n          metric_name, day)                       window_start) reasoning exactly: the dominant read is 'this experiment's\n                                                  per-variant metric curve over time', so the key itself serves the query with\n                                                  no secondary index. experiment_id FIRST is the leftmost-prefix point - it is\n                                                  what lets a single-experiment read jump straight to its rows without\n                                                  touching any other experiment's.\nsrm_checks(experiment_id, checked_at)             'this experiment's most recent SRM check' - the only pattern that ever runs\n                                                  against this table",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
